  "title": "Distinctions and relations",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "2dc3c83c-b338-4c85-abe7-8985ae366a5a",
      "text": "A distinction is a subset of a complex's units that specifies a cause and an effect over subsets of units. Relations are the overlaps among distinctions. Together they make up the cause-effect structure.",
